See, Elric is just one incarnation of Moorcock's Eternal Champion, a
warrior destined to wander the multiverse in many different forms.
Erekose, Corum, Hawkmoon, von Bek, Elric, etc...  Moorcock wrote at
least 30 or more novels and just as many short stories between the early
60s and the early 90s about the Eternal Champion.  Given that some are
published in anthologies, others in collections, and others normally and
that some are out of print or contain overlapping stories, collecting
everything for even a single incarnation of the Champion used to be a
huge, confusing pain.  And to make it even worse, they aren't always
meant to be read in their order of publication.  

Fortunately, essentially all of the Eternal Champion stories have been
collected, organized, and reprinted in a massive 15-volume series of
anthologies.  These volumes are nicely organized according to their main
characters.  So, if you want the Elric stories, just get the Elric
volumes, which happen to be 5 and 11, IIRC.  These two volumes include
all 6 books of the original Elric saga, plus the novels and short
stories that have been published since, reordered to make sense.  :)  

If you really like what you read, feel free to branch out into the other
volumes, of course.  There's plenty there to read.  

